# Project: Zed Raku language extension

A local (and eventually publishable) Zed extension providing real Raku
language support: tree-sitter syntax highlighting, indentation, bracket
matching, outline, text objects, and (optionally) RakuNavigator LSP.

Repo:      ~/Projects/zed-raku
Status:    PLANNED
Owner:     johnm

---

## 1. Background / motivation

- Zed has no Raku (formerly Perl 6) support in the registry or built-ins.
- The only usable tree-sitter grammar is `acrion/tree-sitter-raku`, a fork of
  `tree-sitter-perl` with "initial" Raku adjustments (most notably hyphens in
  identifiers). It ships Helix queries.
- `tree-sitter-perl/zed-perl` is a complete, working Zed language extension
  and is our scaffolding reference.
- Until this lands, Raku files are approximated as Perl via `file_types` in
  `~/.dotfiles/zed/.config/zed/settings.json`.

## 2. Constraints / gotchas (verified 2026-09-19)

- [ ] **Extension id must not contain "zed"/"Zed"/"extension"** (Zed rule).
      Use id `raku`. The repo/dir may be called `zed-raku`.
- [ ] The grammar repo does **not** commit `src/parser.c`; must run
      `tree-sitter generate` (CLI 0.26.9 + Node 26 present).
- [ ] Zed dev extensions require **rustup** + wasm target
      (`wasm32-wasip1`). System Rust is installed but rustup is NOT.
- [ ] Grammar quality caps output: it is a lightly modified Perl grammar, so
      Raku-only syntax (`given/when`, twigils, `role`, `multi`, `subset`,
      junctions, etc.) will mis-highlight until the grammar improves.
- [ ] Grammar is licensed MIT; keep attribution.

## 3. Deliverables

- Local dev extension loaded in Zed via `zed: install dev extension`.
- Syntax highlighting for the Raku file set (see 5.2) + first-line shebang.
- Auto-indent, bracket matching, outline, text objects.
- (Stretch) RakuNavigator LSP integration.
- (Stretch) Published to the Zed extension registry.

## 4. Repo layout (target)

    zed-raku/
      .plan
      README.md
      extension.toml            # id = "raku", pinned grammar rev
      Cargo.toml                # zed_extension_api
      src/
        raku.rs                 # minimal Extension impl
      languages/
        raku/
          config.toml
          highlights.scm
          brackets.scm
          indents.scm
          outline.scm
          injections.scm
          textobjects.scm
      grammar/                  # (option) vendored parser.c, if not forking
      scripts/
        build-grammar.sh        # clone + tree-sitter generate + copy

## 5. Milestones

### M0 - Toolchain
- [ ] Install rustup; `rustup target add wasm32-wasip1`.
- [ ] Confirm `tree-sitter --version`, `node --version`.
- [ ] `git init` in ~/Projects/zed-raku; add .gitignore.

### M1 - Grammar
- [ ] Decide grammar sourcing (pick one):
      a) Fork `acrion/tree-sitter-raku` -> commit generated `parser.c`,
         pin `extension.toml` `[grammars.raku] rev = "<sha>"`.
      b) Vendor grammar locally and use a `file://` repository URL.
      (Prefer (a) for portability; (b) for a fast first pass.)
- [ ] Clone grammar, run `tree-sitter generate`, verify `src/parser.c`.
- [ ] Record upstream rev for reproducibility.

### M2 - Extension scaffold
- [ ] `extension.toml` (id `raku`, name "Raku", schema_version 1, grammars).
- [ ] `Cargo.toml` (copy zed-perl: `zed_extension_api`, cdylib).
- [ ] `src/raku.rs` minimal impl.
- [ ] `languages/raku/config.toml`:
      - name = "Raku", grammar = "raku"
      - path_suffixes = raku, rakumod, rakutest, rakudoc, p6, pl6, pm6, t6, pod6, nqp
      - first_line_pattern for `#!...raku` and `#!...perl6`
      - line_comments = ["# "]
      - autoclose_before + brackets
- [ ] Load via `zed: install dev extension`; sanity check.

### M3 - Queries (bulk of the work)
- [ ] Port `queries/highlights.scm` (Helix) -> Zed capture names.
      Helix and Zed both use @keyword.*, @function, @string, @variable.*,
      @comment, @constant.*; map Helix-only captures as needed.
- [ ] Add `brackets.scm` ("(" @open ")" @close, etc.).
- [ ] Reuse/adapt `indents.scm`.
- [ ] Adapt `textobjects.scm`, `outline.scm`.
- [ ] `injections.scm` for embedded POD (`=begin pod`) if the grammar supports.
- [ ] Manually test against a corpus of real Raku files.

### M4 - LSP (optional / stretch)
- [ ] RakuNavigator (Node) install + build.
- [ ] `[language_servers.raku-navigator]` in extension.toml (language "Raku").
- [ ] Settings for rakuPath + includePaths.

### M5 - Polish / publish (stretch)
- [ ] README, LICENSE, attribution for tree-sitter-perl/-raku.
- [ ] CI to build the grammar/ext (if publishing).
- [ ] Submit to `zed-industries/extensions` (grammar repo must be public with
      committed `parser.c`).

## 6. Test corpus

Collect representative files covering: scripts, modules (`.rakumod`), tests
(`.rakutest`), grammar (`regex`/`grammar`/`token`/`rule`), OO
(`class`/`role`/`method`/`multi`), `given/when`, junctions, twigils,
heredocs, POD, and `nqp`.

## 7. Risks

- Grammar covers Raku only superficially -> highlighting gaps.
- Zed query capture validation is stricter than Helix; unknown captures may
  be ignored or warn.
- rustup requirement adds setup friction; dev extensions build per machine.
- `file://` grammar URLs are machine-specific (dotfiles portability issue).

## 8. Interim approximation (done)

`~/.dotfiles/zed/.config/zed/settings.json` maps the Raku file set listed in
M2 to the existing **Perl** extension. This is intentionally temporary and
should be removed once this extension is installed, to avoid the Perl
extension claiming `.raku` etc.
